IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, Schedules 1 and 2 -- THE CONTRIBUTION RATES BY YEAR.
-- Piece cp6, lines 3101 to 3136 of the Act file.
--
-- Schedule 1 sets the base contribution rate of an employee, an employer and a self-employed person
-- for each year from 1987; Schedule 2 sets the first additional rates (from 2019) and the second
-- additional rates (from 2024). Section 11.1(2) and section 11.2 (piece cp1) send the reader here;
-- section 113.1 (rates-review module) says how the Schedules are amended and deemed amended.
--
-- THE TABLES ARE THE SCHEDULES AS THE DEPOSITED TEXT PRINTS THEM (current to 2026-09-30). An amendment
-- under section 113.1(6), (11.05) or (11.141) changes the printed Schedule, and this module would then
-- need the new rows. Nothing here claims the rows are still current beyond that date.
-- A percentage in the text is written here as a fraction with the percent sign: 1.9 is 1.9%, which is 0.019.
-- A year outside the table (before 1987 for Schedule 1, before 2019 for the first additional rates,
-- before 2024 for the second) is answered NOTHING: the Schedule prints no rate for it.

§ `Schedules 1 and 2 -- contribution rates`

§§ `A row of a Schedule`

-- The three columns of both Schedules, in the order the Schedules print them. The columns are
-- positional, so rows are written below with OF and a ruler comment naming the columns.
DECLARE `cp6 Row of a schedule of contribution rates` HAS
    `schedule rate for employees` IS A NUMBER
    `schedule rate for employers` IS A NUMBER
    `schedule rate for self-employed persons` IS A NUMBER

§§ `Schedule 1 -- contribution rates (base)`

-- src:3101 | SCHEDULE 1 (Subsections 11.1(2) and 113.1(5) and (6), paragraph 113.1(11.05)(b) and subsections 113.1(11.15) and (12))
-- src:3102 | Contribution Rates
-- src:3103 | | For Employees | For Employers | For Self-employed Persons
-- src:3104 | Year | (%) | (%) | (%)
-- src:3105 | 1987 | 1.9 | 1.9 | 3.8
-- src:3106 | 1988 | 2.0 | 2.0 | 4.0
-- src:3107 | 1989 | 2.1 | 2.1 | 4.2
-- src:3108 | 1990 | 2.2 | 2.2 | 4.4
-- src:3109 | 1991 | 2.3 | 2.3 | 4.6
-- src:3110 | 1992 | 2.4 | 2.4 | 4.8
-- src:3111 | 1993 | 2.5 | 2.5 | 5.0
-- src:3112 | 1994 | 2.6 | 2.6 | 5.2
-- src:3113 | 1995 | 2.7 | 2.7 | 5.4
-- src:3114 | 1996 | 2.8 | 2.8 | 5.6
-- src:3115 | 1997 | 3.0 | 3.0 | 6.0
-- src:3116 | 1998 | 3.2 | 3.2 | 6.4
-- src:3117 | 1999 | 3.5 | 3.5 | 7.0
-- src:3118 | 2000 | 3.9 | 3.9 | 7.8
-- src:3119 | 2001 | 4.3 | 4.3 | 8.6
-- src:3120 | 2002 | 4.7 | 4.7 | 9.4
-- src:3121 | 2003 and each subsequent year | 4.95 | 4.95 | 9.9
@ref Act Schedule 1 (src:3101-3121)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `cp6 Row of a schedule of contribution rates`
`Schedule 1 — the row of rates for a year` year MEANS
    --                                                               employees, employers, self-employed
    BRANCH IF year AT MOST 1986 THEN NOTHING
           IF year EQUALS 1987 THEN JUST (`cp6 Row of a schedule of contribution rates` OF 1.9%,  1.9%,  3.8%)
           IF year EQUALS 1988 THEN JUST (`cp6 Row of a schedule of contribution rates` OF 2.0%,  2.0%,  4.0%)
           IF year EQUALS 1989 THEN JUST (`cp6 Row of a schedule of contribution rates` OF 2.1%,  2.1%,  4.2%)
           IF year EQUALS 1990 THEN JUST (`cp6 Row of a schedule of contribution rates` OF 2.2%,  2.2%,  4.4%)
           IF year EQUALS 1991 THEN JUST (`cp6 Row of a schedule of contribution rates` OF 2.3%,  2.3%,  4.6%)
           IF year EQUALS 1992 THEN JUST (`cp6 Row of a schedule of contribution rates` OF 2.4%,  2.4%,  4.8%)
           IF year EQUALS 1993 THEN JUST (`cp6 Row of a schedule of contribution rates` OF 2.5%,  2.5%,  5.0%)
           IF year EQUALS 1994 THEN JUST (`cp6 Row of a schedule of contribution rates` OF 2.6%,  2.6%,  5.2%)
           IF year EQUALS 1995 THEN JUST (`cp6 Row of a schedule of contribution rates` OF 2.7%,  2.7%,  5.4%)
           IF year EQUALS 1996 THEN JUST (`cp6 Row of a schedule of contribution rates` OF 2.8%,  2.8%,  5.6%)
           IF year EQUALS 1997 THEN JUST (`cp6 Row of a schedule of contribution rates` OF 3.0%,  3.0%,  6.0%)
           IF year EQUALS 1998 THEN JUST (`cp6 Row of a schedule of contribution rates` OF 3.2%,  3.2%,  6.4%)
           IF year EQUALS 1999 THEN JUST (`cp6 Row of a schedule of contribution rates` OF 3.5%,  3.5%,  7.0%)
           IF year EQUALS 2000 THEN JUST (`cp6 Row of a schedule of contribution rates` OF 3.9%,  3.9%,  7.8%)
           IF year EQUALS 2001 THEN JUST (`cp6 Row of a schedule of contribution rates` OF 4.3%,  4.3%,  8.6%)
           IF year EQUALS 2002 THEN JUST (`cp6 Row of a schedule of contribution rates` OF 4.7%,  4.7%,  9.4%)
           -- "2003 and each subsequent year"
           OTHERWISE                JUST (`cp6 Row of a schedule of contribution rates` OF 4.95%, 4.95%, 9.9%)

-- The Schedule gives one rate per capacity; the core's Contributing capacity picks the column.
@ref Act Schedule 1 (src:3101-3121)
GIVEN capacity IS A `Contributing capacity`
      year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Schedule 1 — the base contribution rate of a capacity for a year` capacity year MEANS
    CONSIDER `Schedule 1 — the row of rates for a year` year
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST row THEN `Schedules 1 and 2 — the rate of a capacity in a row` capacity row

§§ `Schedule 2 -- first and second additional contribution rates`

-- src:3123 | SCHEDULE 2 First and Second Additional Contribution Rates (Section 11.2 and subsections 113.1(5), (6), (11.141), (11.15) and (12))
-- src:3124 | First Additional Contribution Rates
-- src:3125 | | For Employees | For Employers | For Self-employed Persons
-- src:3126 | Year | (%) | (%) | (%)
-- src:3127 | 2019 | 0.15 | 0.15 | 0.3
-- src:3128 | 2020 | 0.3 | 0.3 | 0.6
-- src:3129 | 2021 | 0.5 | 0.5 | 1.0
-- src:3130 | 2022 | 0.75 | 0.75 | 1.5
-- src:3131 | 2023 | 1.0 | 1.0 | 2.0
-- src:3132 | 2024 and each subsequent year | 1.0 | 1.0 | 2.0
@ref Act Schedule 2, first additional contribution rates (src:3123-3132)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `cp6 Row of a schedule of contribution rates`
`Schedule 2 — the row of first additional rates for a year` year MEANS
    --                                                               employees, employers, self-employed
    BRANCH IF year AT MOST 2018 THEN NOTHING
           IF year EQUALS 2019 THEN JUST (`cp6 Row of a schedule of contribution rates` OF 0.15%, 0.15%, 0.3%)
           IF year EQUALS 2020 THEN JUST (`cp6 Row of a schedule of contribution rates` OF 0.3%,  0.3%,  0.6%)
           IF year EQUALS 2021 THEN JUST (`cp6 Row of a schedule of contribution rates` OF 0.5%,  0.5%,  1.0%)
           IF year EQUALS 2022 THEN JUST (`cp6 Row of a schedule of contribution rates` OF 0.75%, 0.75%, 1.5%)
           IF year EQUALS 2023 THEN JUST (`cp6 Row of a schedule of contribution rates` OF 1.0%,  1.0%,  2.0%)
           -- "2024 and each subsequent year"
           OTHERWISE                JUST (`cp6 Row of a schedule of contribution rates` OF 1.0%,  1.0%,  2.0%)

-- src:3133 | Second Additional Contribution Rates
-- src:3134 | | For Employees | For Employers | For Self-employed Persons
-- src:3135 | Year | (%) | (%) | (%)
-- src:3136 | 2024 and each subsequent year | 4.0 | 4.0 | 8.0
@ref Act Schedule 2, second additional contribution rates (src:3133-3136)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `cp6 Row of a schedule of contribution rates`
`Schedule 2 — the row of second additional rates for a year` year MEANS
    --                                                               employees, employers, self-employed
    BRANCH IF year AT MOST 2023 THEN NOTHING
           -- "2024 and each subsequent year"
           OTHERWISE                JUST (`cp6 Row of a schedule of contribution rates` OF 4.0%,  4.0%,  8.0%)

-- The core's Tier picks the Schedule: the base tier is Schedule 1 and the two additional tiers are
-- the first and second tables of Schedule 2. (Tier is the core's reading of the three contributions
-- that section 2(1) defines; the Schedules are headed by the same three.)
@ref Act Schedule 1, Schedule 2 (src:3101-3136)
GIVEN tier IS A Tier
      capacity IS A `Contributing capacity`
      year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Schedule 1 and 2 — the contribution rate of a tier and a capacity for a year` tier capacity year MEANS
    CONSIDER tier
    WHEN `the base tier` THEN `Schedule 1 — the base contribution rate of a capacity for a year` capacity year
    WHEN `the first additional tier` THEN
        CONSIDER `Schedule 2 — the row of first additional rates for a year` year
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST row THEN `Schedules 1 and 2 — the rate of a capacity in a row` capacity row
    WHEN `the second additional tier` THEN
        CONSIDER `Schedule 2 — the row of second additional rates for a year` year
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST row THEN `Schedules 1 and 2 — the rate of a capacity in a row` capacity row

-- Not a provision: picks the column of a row for a capacity (used by the Schedule 2 lookups).
GIVEN capacity IS A `Contributing capacity`
      row IS A `cp6 Row of a schedule of contribution rates`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Schedules 1 and 2 — the rate of a capacity in a row` capacity row MEANS
    CONSIDER capacity
    WHEN `contributing as an employee` THEN JUST (row's `schedule rate for employees`)
    WHEN `contributing as an employer` THEN JUST (row's `schedule rate for employers`)
    WHEN `contributing as a self-employed person` THEN JUST (row's `schedule rate for self-employed persons`)
